            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Tally to Zoho Books Migration?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Tally to Zoho Books migration transfers all accounting data - ledgers, contacts, invoices, inventory, GST configurations, and opening balances - from desktop-based Tally ERP or TallyPrime into cloud-based Zoho Books, preserving data integrity and enabling real-time financial access for Pune businesses.</p>
<p>For IT firms in Hinjewadi and Kharadi, this means moving years of GST-tagged transactions into a platform accessible from anywhere without VPN. For manufacturing units in Chakan MIDC and MIDC Bhosari, it includes transferring BOM data, multi-location stock records, and vendor payment histories into Zoho Books Inventory modules.</p>
<p>For post-migration bookkeeping, see <a href="/zoho-books-accounting/pune">Zoho Books Accounting in Pune</a>. For businesses continuing with Tally, see <a href="/tally-accounting/pune">Tally Accounting in Pune</a>.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Tally to Zoho Migration:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>Chart of Accounts Migration:</strong> Tally Account Masters mapped to Zoho Books Chart of Accounts with correct grouping hierarchy preserved.</p>
<p><strong>GST Configuration Transfer:</strong> GSTIN, HSN/SAC codes, tax rates, e-invoice settings mapped from Tally GST Masters to Zoho Books GST Settings under CGST Act 2017.</p>
<p><strong>Opening Balance Reconciliation:</strong> Tally Trial Balance matched against imported Zoho Books opening balances - mandatory two-point verification before and after import.</p>
<p><strong>PTRC/PTEC Configuration:</strong> Maharashtra Professional Tax setup in Zoho Books - PTRC for employer salary deductions, PTEC for business professional tax under Maharashtra PT Act 1975.</p>
<p><strong>BOM Migration:</strong> Bill of Materials structure from Tally inventory mapped to Zoho Books composite items with multi-location stock tracking for Chakan MIDC manufacturers.</p>

