<!-- SECTION 15A: LEGAL FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal and Compliance Framework</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>CGST Act, 2017:</strong> Mandates maintenance of accounts and records in electronic form. Zoho Books is GST Suvidha Provider (GSP)-integrated. Automated GSTR-1 and GSTR-2B reconciliation.</p>
<p><strong>Maharashtra PT Act, 1975:</strong> Employers must deduct PTRC from employee salaries. PTEC payable by businesses. PT slabs: Rs 200/month (Rs 10,001-15,000), Rs 300/month (Rs 15,001-20,000), Rs 400/month (Rs 20,001+). Source: mahagst.gov.in.</p>
<p><strong>Income Tax Act, 1961:</strong> Section 44AA requires specified professions to maintain books of accounts. Zoho Books exports accepted as valid books.</p>
<p><strong>Companies Act, 2013:</strong> Companies under RoC Pune must maintain accurate books for statutory audit. Zoho Books financial statements are audit-compatible under Rule 3 of Companies (Accounts) Rules, 2014.</p>
<p><strong>Key Portals:</strong> <a href="https://www.gst.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gst.gov.in</a> | <a href="https://mahagst.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mahagst.gov.in</a> | <a href="https://www.mca.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mca.gov.in</a></p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

